            "title": "Broken Windows absolute path check",
            "severity": "medium",
            "file": "lib/utils.js",
            "line": 70,
            "explanation": "The change removes support for Windows absolute paths with a forward slash (e.g., 'c:/foo'), checking only for backslash (e.g., 'c:\\foo'). This breaks detection of valid absolute paths on Windows that use forward slashes, which are commonly accepted by Node.js and many libraries.",
            "suggestion": "Restore the check to include both backslash and forward slash in position 2 after drive letter. For example: if (':' === path[1] && ('\\' === path[2] || '/' === path[2])) return true;",
            "failureAfterChange": "Input path 'c:/folder/file.txt' returns false from isAbsolute(), incorrectly treated as relative path instead of absolute.",
